      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "عَنْ حَمَّادِ بْنِ عُثْمَانَ فَقَدْ رَوَيْتُهُ عَنْ أَبِي رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ عَنْ سَعْدِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ وَ الْحِمْيَرِيِّ جَمِيعًا عَنْ يَعْقُوبَ بْنِ يَزِيدَ عَنْ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ أَبِي عُمَيْرٍ عَنْ حَمَّادِ بْنِ عُثْمَانَ",
        "translations": {
          "en": "from Ḥammād ibn ʿUthmān, then I have narrated it from my father—may Allah be pleased with him—from Saʿd ibn ʿAbdillāh and al-Ḥimyārī together, from Yaʿqūb ibn Yazīd, from Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿUmayr, from Ḥammād ibn ʿUthmān."
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This passage clarifies the sanad/isnad by which the author transmits narrations from Ḥammād ibn ʿUthmān in Man Lā Yaḥḍuruhu al-Faqīh. Its significance lies in documenting the precise chain of transmission and preserving hadith provenance.",
      "seo_question": "What is the transmission chain of Shaykh al-Ṣadūq to Ḥammād ibn ʿUthmān in Man Lā Yaḥḍuruhu al-Faqīh?",
      "key_terms": {
        "رَوَيْتُهُ": "I transmitted it",
        "أَبِي": "my father, through whom the transmission passes",
        "جَمِيعًا": "together; indicating joint transmission by two narrators",
        "حَمَّادِ بْنِ عُثْمَانَ": "the transmitter to whom this chain leads"
      }
    }
  },
